/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  yesterday -- A PRIOR: yesterday's reconciled flows, with the uncertainty
  they are given after a day of drift.  SYNTHETIC.

  The values close every balance, as yesterday's answer did: 99.6 + 49.4 =
  149.0 through the mixer and the reactor, 149.0 = 89.5 + 59.5 at the
  separator, 59.5 = 10.1 + 49.4 at the splitter.  The sigmas are an
  author's choice, 2 % of each flow, stated as one: how far a flow may
  have moved overnight is a judgement about the plant, not a number any
  meter supplies.

  Each prior is INDEPENDENT of the others -- the operation accepts a
  diagonal prior only, and says so on the run.  Yesterday's reconciled
  flows were in fact correlated (they closed the balances together); that
  information is deliberately not carried.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

F1 { value  99.6 t/h; sigma 2.0 t/h; }
F2 { value 149.0 t/h; sigma 3.0 t/h; }
F3 { value 149.0 t/h; sigma 3.0 t/h; }
F4 { value  89.5 t/h; sigma 1.8 t/h; }
F5 { value  59.5 t/h; sigma 1.2 t/h; }
F6 { value  10.1 t/h; sigma 0.2 t/h; }
F7 { value  49.4 t/h; sigma 1.0 t/h; }
